    "image.report.preparation-intro": "Both models use the same cleaned data and splits. Cleaning and splitting precede augmentation; original images are decoded and transformed when passed to the model.",
    "image.report.cleaning-title": "Decode, audit, and clean images",
    "image.report.decode-step": "Fully decode images with PIL to detect reading errors. Correct EXIF orientation before measuring characteristics or hashing, then convert to RGB for a consistent three-channel input. The audit retains the original color mode.",
    "image.report.audit-step": "Check that labels are 0–5 for the six classes, and record sample IDs, size, color, brightness, contrast, and Laplacian variance. All 17,034 images decode successfully and have valid labels, so none are removed for decoding errors or invalid labels.",
    "image.report.hash-step": "Compute SHA-256 from size and RGB pixels after orientation correction and before resize/crop. This detects identical pixels even when filenames differ, rather than relying only on filenames or compressed-file hashes.",
    "image.report.clean-step": "Retain the valid test set unchanged. For train, first remove images duplicating test, then all images in hash groups with conflicting labels, then retain one image in each same-label duplicate group. The log records 3 test duplicates, 20 images in conflicting-label groups, and 5 same-label copies removed: 28 in total. Labels are not reassigned automatically.",
    "image.report.partition-title": "Split data and check leakage",
    "image.report.partition": "Cleaning leaves 14,006 original training images (14,034 − 28). train_test_split with test_size=0.20, label stratification, and random_state=42 creates 11,204 training and 2,802 validation images, approximately preserving development-set class proportions. The original test set retains 3,000 images; the three splits total 17,006.",
    "image.report.split-roles": "Train updates weights. Validation selects checkpoints by macro-F1, controls early stopping, and evaluates proposed preprocessing. Test measures final performance after choices are fixed; earlier test auditing checks only structure, quality, and duplicates.",
    "image.report.transforms-intro": "Both models use the same training augmentation. Validation/test use each model’s IMAGENET1K_V1 weights.transforms(), with the same resize/crop sizes and normalization constants. The table lists steps in order after RGB decoding.",
